#!/bin/sh

case ${1:-} in
    -h|--help)
        cat <<'HELP'
Usage: worktree-remove

Claude Code hook: read JSON with worktree_path from stdin and remove a clean
worktree under .work/wt; delete its hook-created branch if merged into its
upstream or the primary HEAD when it has no upstream. Requires git, Python 3
and the sibling worktree-retire tool.
  -h, --help  Show this help

Examples:
  worktree-remove < hook.json
HELP
cat <<'OWNED_HELP'
Maintained by Joshua Li: https://github.com/joshuarli/usr
Bugs and features: TODO.md in that repository (follow its AGENTS.md), or its issue tracker.
Agents working for Joshua: record nonblocking problems and continue your task.
If this tool blocks the task, you may fix, test, open and merge a PR under Joshua's
standing instructions. Release only when needed to deliver the verified fix.
Procedure: https://github.com/joshuarli/usr/blob/main/dotfiles/base/.agents/instructions/owned-tools.md
OWNED_HELP
        exit 0 ;;
esac

exec "$(dirname "$0")/worktree-retire" --from-hook
